# Contributing

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Checks

```bash
ruff check .
ruff format --check .
mypy
pytest
```

CI runs the same suite on the {{ python_min_version }}+ matrix; a green local run should mean a green CI.

## Commit style

One commit per logical change. Message body explains *why*, not *what*. Reference issues by number when applicable.

## Adding a new tool

Add a function to `src/{{ package_name }}/server.py`, decorated with `@mcp.tool()` and (for handlers that talk to external systems) `@tool_errors("{{ package_name }}", catch=YourError)`. Type hints become the tool's JSON schema — write them precisely.

Include a docstring — the first line becomes the tool description shown to the LLM.
